# Database checks

These scripts test the SQL functions, row-level security and concurrency of the self-hosted database. They read `SUPABASE_DB_URL` and the Supabase keys from `.env.qa`, the separate test backend (`npm run setup -- --qa`), never the owner's `.env`.

## Migrations and regressions

`npm run test:db` runs the migration replay below and then every opt-in `*.live.test.ts`, one file at a time.

```sh
node supabase/tests/migrations.mjs
```

Replays every migration into a temporary schema, compares it with the current schema (columns, constraints, indexes, RLS, policies, views, triggers, functions), and runs the `.sql` regression fixtures on both. Everything runs in rollback-only transactions; migration history stays unchanged and the temporary schema is removed.

`workspace-isolation.sql` seeds two synthetic users with records in every application table and checks, as the `authenticated` role, that neither can see or change the other's data. Keep its fixtures and RPC cases in step when adding tables or mutations.

Single regressions run with their `run-*.mjs` script, for example `node supabase/tests/run-goal-reservations.mjs`. `run-sql.mjs` runs the import-review fixture.

## Concurrency

`*-concurrency.mjs` scripts (chat, imports, reviews, recurring occurrences, reservations) open separate authenticated and service connections to check locks, cancellation and duplicate claims. They create synthetic users or a disposable schema, remove them by exact ID, and leave a recovery note in ignored `.qa/` files if interrupted.

## Live checks

- `precision.mjs` reads Money and budget pages through PostgREST with amounts beyond JavaScript's safe integer range.
- `summary-live.mjs` (with the app running) checks scheduled summaries end to end: dispatch, deduplication per period, cancellation and disabling.
- `lib/schema.live.test.ts` checks the migrated database itself: `lib/schema.ts` lists the same tables and columns, the app and `currency_minor_digits` agree on every currency, and no function raises a conflict as `40001`.
- Opt-in unit tests compare SQL with application logic, for example `RUN_RESERVATION_DB_TESTS=1 npm test -- lib/finance/reservation-balance.live.test.ts` (PowerShell: `$env:RUN_RESERVATION_DB_TESTS='1'` first).

None of these touch the owner's workspace. Migrations themselves are applied by `npm run setup`.
do $$
declare
  u uuid := gen_random_uuid(); w uuid; c uuid := gen_random_uuid();
  a uuid := gen_random_uuid(); t uuid := gen_random_uuid(); r uuid := gen_random_uuid(); r2 uuid := gen_random_uuid();
  result jsonb; completion text;
begin
  insert into auth.users(id,email) values(u,'qa-'||u||'@example.invalid');
  select id into strict w from public.workspaces where owner_id=u;
  perform set_config('request.jwt.claim.sub',u::text,true);
  insert into public.conversations(id,workspace_id,title) values(c,w,'Synthetic chat');
  insert into public.accounts(id,workspace_id,name,currency_code) values(a,w,'Synthetic cash','EUR');
  insert into public.transactions(id,workspace_id,account_id,posted_on,description,amount_minor,currency_code) values(t,w,a,'2026-10-01','Synthetic',-100,'EUR');
  result := public.start_chat_request(r,c,'Set category of transaction '||t||' to "Groceries"','{}');
  if result->>'started' <> 'true' then raise exception 'First request must claim execution'; end if;
  result := public.start_chat_request(r,c,'Set category of transaction '||t||' to "Groceries"','{}');
  if result->>'started' <> 'false' then raise exception 'Duplicate request must not claim execution'; end if;
  perform public.chat_set_category(r,t,'Groceries');
  perform public.chat_set_category(r,t,'Groceries');
  if (select count(*) from public.correction_events where transaction_id=t) <> 1 then raise exception 'Duplicate model writes must create one correction'; end if;
  perform public.cancel_chat_request(r);
  begin
    perform public.chat_set_category(r,t,'Groceries');
    raise exception 'Canceled requests must prevent writes';
  exception when sqlstate '57014' then null;
  end;
  -- The prose-chat contract allows owned completion, but cancellation still fences it.
  completion := public.finish_chat_request(r,'completed','Late owner answer');
  if completion <> 'canceled' then raise exception 'Owner completion must retain cancellation'; end if;
  if exists(select 1 from public.messages where reply_to=r) then raise exception 'Canceled owner completion must not publish'; end if;
  perform set_config('request.jwt.claim.role','service_role',true);
  perform public.finish_verified_chat_request(r,u,w,'Late answer',array[]::uuid[],array[]::text[],null);
  perform set_config('request.jwt.claim.role','authenticated',true);
  if exists(select 1 from public.messages where reply_to=r) then raise exception 'Canceled request must not save late replies'; end if;
  perform public.start_chat_request(r2,c,'Change my Amazon to Groceries','{}');
  begin
    perform public.chat_set_category(r2,t,'Groceries');
    raise exception 'Ambiguous prose must not authorize a model target';
  exception when sqlstate '22023' then null;
  end;
  perform set_config('request.jwt.claim.sub',gen_random_uuid()::text,true);
  begin
    perform public.finish_chat_request(r2,'completed','Foreign reply');
    raise exception 'Foreign workspace completion must be refused';
  exception when sqlstate 'P0002' then null;
  end;
  begin
    perform public.cancel_chat_request(r2);
    raise exception 'Foreign workspace cancellation must be refused';
  exception when sqlstate 'P0002' then null;
  end;

